### Q2. Deterministic Factoring

- **Best unconditional claim is unchanged:** worst-case $O(N^{1/5}\log^{16/5}N/(\log\log N)^{3/5})$ (Harvey–Hittmeir 2022 `[KNOWN]`) and average-case $O(N^{1/6}(\log N)^{c+1}\log\log N)$ over balanced semiprimes (`Theorem AV`, [avgtime_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/avgtime_results.md#L17-L26) §0, already unconditional, unrefereed `[proved]`). **Nothing subexponential becomes deterministic** `[proved]`.
- **Why:** Dirichlet GRH discharges Miller splitting (`Prop PIN`) and makes `Theorem DZ` (`DSR_α ⇒ deterministic L_N[α]`) unconditional, while `Lemma XK-Z` and `DD1`/`WR` deterministically handle algebraic elimination and $\mathbb{Q}$-rank ([zroute_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/zroute_results.md#L135-L220) §2, §4–§5) `[proved]`. The entire bottleneck is **`Hypothesis DSR_α`** (constructing smooth splits for $q^H \bmod N$): `Theorem SB` rules out black-box JMV-walk derandomisers, `Theorem FN` rules out Bach/Fourier-norm certificates ($\|1_{S_{\text{can}}}\|_A' \ge N^{1/2-o(1)}$), and `Prop BOX-∞` rules out short positive multiplier boxes ([dsr_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/dsr_results.md#L30-L58) §0, §2–§3) `[proved]`. In the exponential worst case, GRH character sums hit the Parseval cap $\delta \le 4/25 < 7/25$ and do not beat $N^{1/5}$ (`Lemma M`, `Theorem B`, [cov38b_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/cov38b_results.md#L305-L315) §2.1) `[proved]`.

---

### Q3. Rigorous-Randomised Side

- **Re-examining `nested Prop R2`:** `Prop R2` ([nested_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/nested_results.md#L332-L358) §4) only floors designs *without algebraic children* at $2/5$ `[heuristic]`. `nested` assumed algebraic children required joint control of $>d+1$ points (`Lemma OD`, `#L362-L398`). Phases 25–31 bypassed `Lemma OD` at depth 2 **without GRH** via union-bound + parent-count decoupling (`Prop UB`, `Prop DC`, [pc3_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/pc3_results.md#L128-L166) §2), reaching $L[\alpha]$ for $\alpha \in (3/8, 2/5)$ and $L[3/8]$ ($a>2c_2$) from published inputs (`Theorem 2L-MF`, [mf2L_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/mf2L_results.md#L56-L60) §0; conditional on the internal chain + `audit2L`'s `U′`-under-`DW` write-up) `[proved]`.
- **What GRH does and does not discharge:**
  - *At $2/5$ & $[3/8, 2/5)$:* `Theorem U-MF` ([mfU_theorem.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/mfU_theorem.md#L60-L65) §0) and `2L-MF` ([mf2L_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/mf2L_results.md#L46-L55) §0) are already GRH-free. Dirichlet GRH simplifies small-conductor character twists `Hyp SC` (already proved via Drappeau CJM 2015), and Dedekind GRH simplifies characters (`Lemma X_ERH`); neither changes any exponent or removes the combinatorial squarefree-part condition $a > 2c_2$ at $3/8$ ([thmAB_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/thmAB_results.md#L174) §1.3) `[proved]`.
  - *Below $3/8$ ($4/11$ and depth $j \ge 4$):* **GRH does not push below $3/8$** `[proved]`. Depth-$i$ decoupling requires relative variance $\phi_i \le \eta_i \asymp D^{-i\alpha}$ ([pc3_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/pc3_results.md#L348-L355) §7.5), but the *principal-character* (archimedean + gcd-factor $\tau(\delta)$) variance is $\Omega(\gamma^2\lambda^2) = \Omega(D^{-2\alpha})$ even with zero character error (`Lemmas LF-A, OPV-A`, [thmAB_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/thmAB_results.md#L379-L413) §6). Thus $4/11$ ($i=2$) stays borderline and $j \ge 4$ ($i \ge 3$) fails regardless of GRH `[heuristic]`.
  - *Rigorous $L[1/3]$ NFS:* **Still conditional** `[proved]`. GRH discharges neither `Hyp AD` in `nested Theorem NR` ([nested_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/nested_results.md#L485-L500) §8) nor 2-adic Bockstein fruitfulness (`Conjecture F` / LV `Conj 7.1`, [fruit_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/fruit_results.md#L64-L75) §0; [detGRH_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/detGRH_results.md#L299-L308) §3). *New angle under Dirichlet GRH:* applying `zroute`'s proved `Lemma XK-Z` + `Prop PIN` ([zroute_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/zroute_results.md#L135-L155) §2, `#L312-L315` §3.2) to Lee–Venkatesan's unconditional randomized $L[1/3]$ relations ([README.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/README.md#L17-L18)) replaces 2-adic `Conj 7.1` by **rational $\mathbb{Q}$-pinning (`PIN` on $q < 2\ln^2 N$)** summed across $L[1/3]$ independent LV fields `[proved]` — still unproved (`zroute-2`), but avoids 2-adic sign obstructions `[speculative]`.

---

### Q4. Below $L[1/3]$: Theorem vs. Sketched Method

- **GRH-as-theorem touches none of the five open doors positively** `[proved]`:
  - `grdeg` relative-rank $\ge 3$ type-D ([grdeg_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/grdeg_results.md#L66-L80) §0) & $G_r \to L[1/4]$ model ([midk_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/midk_results.md#L39-L65) §0): Diophantine height / infinite-unit-volume ($V_F=\infty$) geometry; zero-free strips neither construct degenerate modules nor bound unit orbits.
  - `Prop SI` ($L[1/3, 1.2114]$, [suffmap_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/suffmap_results.md#L318-L343) §1.4; [sicheck_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/sicheck_results.md#L538-L596) §5): Constant-only ($\alpha=1/3$); RH short-interval smoothness stops at $h \ge X^{1/2+\varepsilon}$ (`genus2rh` §6.2), far above $L_X[2/3] = X^{o(1)}$, and gives existence, not an $L^{o(1)}$ CVP constructor ([siconstruct_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/siconstruct_results.md#L92-L155) §2.1).
  - Single $a_f(N)$ ([cuspcoef_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/cuspcoef_results.md#L196) §2.2, `#L379-L392` §5): GRH tightens the `Theorem DFB` barrier ($B=O(\log\log p)$); native cost stays $\ge N^{1/2+o(1)}$.
  - `PRIM` ([prim_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/prim_results.md#L338-L346) §3, `#L672`; [completeness_audit_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/completeness_audit_results.md#L225-L235) §5.4): GRH only bounds fixed-base exceptional primes (a barrier, defeated at large height); $O(1)$-bit leaks remain exponential (`caudit` §7 Q4).
- **Can `remark.pdf`'s *method* ($\sqrt{X}$ theta lifts, Guinand–Weil variance, path quadric, Bost slope) convert into useful tools?**
  - *Smooth numbers near $kN$ (`Prop SI`):* **No** `[heuristic]`. Spectral bandwidth $X/h \approx X^{1-o(1)}$ is dominated by *on-line* ($\operatorname{Re}\rho=1/2$) diagonal variance ($\sqrt{X}$ lifts amplify off-line zeros, not on-line noise), and explicit-formula positivity is non-constructive ([conn_ana.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/conn_ana.md#L36) P2; [siconstruct_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/siconstruct_results.md#L299) §3).
  - *Smooth BDH / pair correlation:* **No sub-$1/3$ gain** `[proved]`. Finite-depth ladders satisfy $\alpha_j > 1/3$ ([midk_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/midk_results.md#L126-L133) §1.2), and depth $\ge 4$ dies on principal-character variance $D^{-2\alpha}$.
  - *Character/point-count bounds beating Burgess:* **No sub-$1/3$ gain** `[proved]`. GRH *already* beats Burgess down to polylog length, and `dsr` (`Thm FN`/`SB`) + `cov38b` (`Lemma M`/`Thm B`) prove character-sum bounds neither solve `DSR` nor beat $N^{1/5}$ via phase discarding. (Path-quadric $x_1x_2+\dots+x_{k-1}x_k$ seesaw sums faintly resemble `cov38b`'s **phase-retaining 26th-moment** target at $q^{0.32}$ ([cov38b_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/cov38b_results.md#L404-L407) §2.4), which is exponential $<N^{1/5}$ only `[speculative]`.)
  - **Single most promising conversion touching sub-$L[1/3]$ (`grdeg` door (i), *barrier direction*):** **Bost's Arakelov slope inequality** (`[KNOWN]` theorem, usable whether or not `remark.pdf` holds) applied to evaluation kernels on rank-$m \ge 3$ $\mathcal{O}_k$-bundles to bypass infinite unit volume ($V_F=\infty$) `[speculative]`. *Statement needed:* For any rank-$m \ge 3$ $\mathcal{O}_k$-submodule of $\mathcal{O}_K \times \mathcal{O}_{K'}$ ($[k:\mathbb{Q}]=e$, $r=me$, $[K:k]=n$) with $m-1$ mod-$N$ links not confined to a lower-rank sublattice, $\max_j h_k(w_j) \ge c(r/D)\log N - O(dn)$ ($c>0$), closing `grdeg` door (i) from model $L[1/4]$ back to $\alpha \ge 1/3$ ([grdeg_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/grdeg_results.md#L66-L80) §0).

