### Q5. Verdict & Top Three Next Threads

- **Verdict:** **No credible path below $L[1/3]$** ($P < 1\text{–}2\%$) `[heuristic]`. Neither GRH/ERH nor `remark.pdf`'s method lowers candidate sizes below the resultant/size–entropy floor ([suffmap_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/suffmap_results.md#L158-L195) Thm SS, `#L674` H14; [completeness_audit_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/completeness_audit_results.md#L62-L69) §0).
- **Ranked next threads:**
  1. **Consolidate unconditional rigorous $L[3/8]$ (`U′` under `DW` + clean `2L-MF` note):**
     - *Target:* Write out `Hyp U′` under design `DW` (`audit2L` open item) and merge `thmAB` + `Lemma SPR-P′` + `mf2L` ([README.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/README.md#L103-L106); [STATUS.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/STATUS.md)).
     - *Remark relevance:* **None** — already unconditional from published inputs `[proved]`.
     - *Probability / Cost:* **~80%**; **Low** (1–2 rounds).
  2. **Close `grdeg` door (i) via Bost's Arakelov slope inequality over $\mathcal{O}_k$:**
     - *Target:* Prove $\max_j h_k(w_j) \ge c(r/D)\log N - O(dn)$ for non-sublattice-confined type-D modules ($m \ge 3$), testing first on codex's $k=\mathbb{Q}(i), r=6$ witness ([grdeg_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/grdeg_results.md#L264-L268) §8).
     - *Remark relevance:* **Method-inspired only** — uses published Bost/Chambert-Loir slope inequalities, independent of `remark.pdf` `[speculative]`.
     - *Probability / Cost:* **~30%** to close door (i) ($<2\%$ for a sub-$1/3$ algorithm); **Low–Medium** (1 round).
  3. **Conditional rigorous Las Vegas $L_N[1/3]$ via pooled LV fields + `XK-Z` + `Prop PIN`:**
     - *Target:* Under explicit Dirichlet GRH, test and try to prove `Prop PIN` ($e_q \in \sum_{j=1}^J W_j$ for $q < 2\ln^2 N$) across $J = L_N[1/3, c']$ independent Lee–Venkatesan fields ([zroute_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/zroute_results.md#L211-L220) §2, `#L312-L315` §3.2) `[speculative]`.
     - *Remark relevance:* **High if Dirichlet GRH holds** — yields `Dirichlet GRH ⇒ rigorous L[1/3]` (valuable conditionally even if `remark.pdf` fails `[KNOWN]`).
     - *Probability / Cost:* **~10–15%**; **Medium** (1 toy-pooling + 1 switching round).

